---@class aws.bedrock_agent.GetRetrievalInstructionRequest
---@field retrievalInstructionId aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionId The identifier of the retrieval instruction to get.
---@field retrievalInstructionVersion? aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionVersionSelector The version to return: a version number, or DRAFT for the retrieval instruction's current reviewed content. When omitted, DRAFT is used. This default is permanent: omitting retrievalInstructionVersion will never resolve to a numbered version.

---@class aws.bedrock_agent.GetRetrievalInstructionResponse
---@field retrievalInstructionId aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionId The identifier of the retrieval instruction.
---@field retrievalInstructionArn aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionArn The ARN of the retrieval instruction.
---@field name distilled.Secret The name of the retrieval instruction.
---@field status aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionStatus Specifies whether you can use the instruction. You can resolve only an ACTIVE instruction at retrieval time. Monotone: INACTIVE to ACTIVE once, never back. Numbered versions are always ACTIVE.
---@field lastTransitionStatus aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionLastTransitionStatus The outcome or in-progress state of the most recent create or update. CREATING or UPDATING means the operation is still running. Independent of status. Always has a value from the create 202 onward. On a numbered version this is always CREATE_SUCCESSFUL: a version is created once, from reviewed content, and is immutable.
---@field instruction? distilled.Secret The reviewed content this instruction serves — what AgenticRetrieveStream resolves while status is ACTIVE. Absent until the first create review passes. Always present on a numbered version.
---@field createdAt aws.bedrock_agent.DateTimestamp When the retrieval instruction was created. On a numbered version, when that version was created.
---@field updatedAt aws.bedrock_agent.DateTimestamp When the retrieval instruction was last updated. Equal to createdAt on a numbered version, which is immutable.
---@field description? distilled.Secret A description of the retrieval instruction. On a numbered version, the description of that version.
---@field customerEncryptionKeyArn? aws.bedrock_agent.KmsKeyArn The ARN of the customer managed KMS key protecting this content, when one was supplied at create.
---@field lastTransitionStatusReasons? aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionFailureReasons Why the most recent create or update was rejected. One entry for each rejected field, or a single entry when the review itself failed. Each entry has a machine-readable code and a message, and names the field when it applies to one. The service includes this field only when lastTransitionStatus is CREATE_FAILED or UPDATE_FAILED. Never present on a numbered version.
---@field version? aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionVersionSelector The version this response describes: a version number, or DRAFT.
---@field latestVersion? aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionNumericalVersion The largest version number that currently exists for this retrieval instruction, that is, the newest version you can retrieve. Present only on a DRAFT read, and only when at least one version exists. Because version numbers are never reused, deleting versions can leave gaps: this is the newest existing version, not a count and not the highest number ever created.

