---The name of a retrieval instruction.
---@alias aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionName string

---A retrieval instruction version number: at most nine digits (1 to 999,999,999). Numbers are allocated monotonically from 1 and never reused, even after the version is deleted, so the shape also bounds the lifetime number of versions an instruction can ever allocate.
---@alias aws.bedrock_agent.RetrievalInstructionNumericalVersion string

---Specifies whether you can use a retrieval instruction. You can resolve only an ACTIVE retrieval instruction at retrieval time. Monotone: INACTIVE to ACTIVE once, never back.
